Aim

To create and manage virtual machines in Oracle Cloud by configuring operating systems and monitoring performance.

Requirements
Oracle Cloud Account
Internet Connection
SSH Client (PowerShell or PuTTY)
Step 1: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open:

Oracle Cloud Console

Enter:

Username
Password

Click:

Sign In

Step 2: Open Compute Service

Click:

☰ Menu
→ Compute
→ Instances

Step 3: Create New Virtual Machine

Click:

Create Instance

Step 4: Configure Instance Details

Fill:

Field	Value
Name	MyVM
Compartment	MyLabCompartment
Step 5: Select Operating System

Under:

Image and Shape

Click:

Edit

Choose:

Image = Oracle Linux

Click:

Select Image

Step 6: Select Shape

Click:

Change Shape

Choose:

VM.Standard.E2.1.Micro
(Always Free Eligible)

Click:

Select Shape

Step 7: Configure Networking

Keep default VCN settings.

Ensure:

Assign Public IPv4 Address = Enabled
Step 8: Add SSH Keys

Under:

Add SSH Keys

Select:

Generate a key pair for me

Download:

Private Key
Public Key

Store safely.

Step 9: Create Virtual Machine

Click:

Create

Wait 2–5 minutes.

Status changes to:

Running

Step 10: Copy Public IP Address

Open instance page.

Copy:

Public IP Address

Example:

152.xxx.xxx.xxx
Step 11: Connect to VM Using SSH

Open PowerShell.

Run:

ssh -i privatekey.key opc@your_public_ip

Example:

ssh -i ssh-key.key opc@152.xxx.xxx.xxx

Type:

yes

Connected successfully.

Step 12: Check System Information

Run:

uname -a

Check memory:

free -m

Check disk:

df -h
Step 13: Monitor CPU Usage

Run:

top

This displays:

CPU usage
Memory usage
Running processes

Press:

q

to exit.

Step 14: Restart Virtual Machine

Go to OCI Console.

Click:

More Actions
→ Reboot

Wait for restart.

Step 15: Stop Virtual Machine

Click:

Stop

Instance status changes to:

Stopped

Step 16: Start Virtual Machine Again

Click:

Start

VM becomes active again.

Step 17: Delete Virtual Machine (Optional)

Click:

Terminate

Select:

Permanently Delete Attached Boot Volume

Click:

Terminate Instance

Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Created virtual machine
Configured operating system
Connected using SSH
Monitored system performance
Restarted and stopped VM

Virtual machine management completed successfully.
